@@ -580,3 +580,30 @@ MCP, or session-resume behavior.
 - [Plugin SDK overview](/plugins/sdk-overview) - registration API reference
 - [Plugin manifest](/plugins/manifest) - `cliBackends` and setup descriptors
 - [Agent harness](/plugins/sdk-agent-harness) - full external agent runtimes
+
+## Agent-specific native permission profiles
+
+A backend normalizer receives the admitted `agentId` and `workspaceDir`. Its
+optional `toolsAllow` cap selects exact OpenClaw tools with native tools disabled;
+OpenClaw intersects it with the caller allowance and the scoped MCP catalog.
+An empty cap stays empty. `strictClearEnv` makes the backend's `clearEnv` exclusions
+apply even when an environment-preservation override is present.
+
+The bundled Claude backend can opt into `nativePermissionMode: "defer"` through
+an explicit Anthropic `cliProfiles` entry. It tags native authorization requests
+with `phase: "pre-tool"` or `"permission"`. A passing pre-tool check continues
+Claude's permission evaluation. A permission escalation uses OpenClaw's existing
+allow-once/deny approval and ignores standing grants and automatic allow modes.
+Host vetoes, rewritten input and current-run checks remain in force. Other
+backends and unselected agents retain their existing contract.
+
+Configure `plugins.entries.anthropic.config.cliConfigDir` for the dedicated native
+subscription login and `cliProfiles` keyed by agent ID. `workspace` uses native
+file tools and sandboxed shell commands rooted at the admitted workspace.
+`diagnostic` explicitly retains unsandboxed diagnostic access. `restricted` needs
+an explicit non-wildcard agent `tools.allow` and uses the existing MCP-only path.
+Optional `protectedPaths` adds absolute denied paths to native workspace profiles.
+These profiles require Claude Code 2.1.301 or newer and reject forwarded API
+credentials. They exclude ambient settings and clear inherited service secrets.
+Managed Claude settings still require deployment qualification because they can
+have higher precedence than inline settings.
